[04:27:11] ## What changed
[04:27:11] **`frontend/src/crafting/ResolutionTreeNode.vue`** — each requirement is now a compact summary: its own item icon/name (ID fallback kept), the supplied `{n} needed`, one chip per *supplied* acquisition method (a mixed requirement keeps `From stock` **and** `Bought`), the named character under `Crafted by …`, and the three inclusive costs on one labelled line. Every supplied state and blocked reason keeps its marker and sentence, so `PRICE_UNAVAILABLE`, `UNVALUED_NONTRADEABLE`, `NON_TRADEABLE_MATERIAL` and unrecognized codes still appear and still name their own item. Children sit in a **collapsed** native `<details>`/`<summary>` at every level including the root's; expanding one opens nothing beneath it, and the whole tree stays in the DOM, so collapsing withholds no requirement.
[04:27:11] **`frontend/src/crafting/CraftingResolution.vue`** — the introductory paragraph became one line ("A separate calculation of one output batch — not every craft the table counted."), the `THIS RECIPE IN THAT FRESH CALCULATION` block is gone, and the tree is keyed on a counter bumped per accepted answer so a replaced selection remounts collapsed rather than inheriting expansions.
[04:27:11] Removed per-node rows: stock/crafted/bought/missing, producing recipe + ID, crafts run, produced total, `Character`. All those fields remain in the DTOs and the response — no contract field, calculation, request or association rule was touched.
[04:27:11] **Economic rows (AC4):** all three costs retained unchanged in value — none is derivable from the other two, `—` and `0c` stay distinct. What was removed is their three-row grid and the paragraph repeated under every node; the two statements they need are now made once under the tree. On the live evidence tree that dropped 15 rows and 5 paragraphs, losing no figure.
[04:27:11] Both components are shared with Discovery, which therefore inherits the same presentation.
